<section class="section">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <div style="margin-top: var(--space-5);">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I buy a home on a temporary skilled visa?</button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, but with FIRB approval, and only a new home, off-the-plan or land until 30 June 2029. A smaller group of lenders will lend.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Do permanent residents pay foreign buyer surcharges?</button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>In most states, no. NSW is the main exception: PR holders also need to meet its 200-day test. Check the state table.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I buy an established home with my Australian partner?</button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, if you buy as joint tenants and your partner is a citizen, PR or eligible NZ citizen. No FIRB approval is needed.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">I'm on a student visa. Can I get a home loan?</button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Realistically, very hard. Mainstream lenders generally don't lend to student, graduate or working holiday visa holders.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is FIRB the same as stamp duty?</button>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>No. FIRB is federal approval to buy. Stamp duty and its foreign buyer surcharges are state taxes. You may need to deal with both.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ── CTA ── #}
